>## @requirement usesSimpleNotFullMapping toUpper uses the simple (one-to-one) Unicode case mapping, not full case folding: a code point with no single-code-point uppercase mapping (e.g. sharp s, n preceded by apostrophe) is returned unchanged rather than expanded to a multi-code-point full mapping, and a code point whose simple mapping is itself a different single code point maps to that code point.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
